{"name":"Violet Tulip","hex":"#9e91c3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"violet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant or flower of the genus Viola, especially the fragrant Viola odorata;  similar-looking plants and flowers.","A person thought to resemble V. odorata, especially in its beauty and delicacy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a violet colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet"},{"term":"tulip","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of flowering plant, genus Tulipa.","The flower of this plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tulip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tulip","blocks":[{"text":"Tulips are spring-blooming perennial herbaceous bulbiferous geophytes in the Tulipa genus. Their flowers are usually large, showy, and brightly coloured, generally red, orange, pink, yellow, or white. They often have a different coloured blotch at the base of the tepals, internally. Because of a degree of variability within the populations and a long history of cultivation, classification has been complex and controversial. The tulip is a member of the lily family, Liliaceae, along with 14 other genera, where it is most closely related to Amana, Erythronium, and Gagea in the tribe Lilieae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/%D7%A6%D7%91%D7%A2%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%9D.JPG/330px-%D7%A6%D7%91%D7%A2%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%9D.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tulip","wikidata":"Q93201"},{"title":"Violet (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Violet is the color of light at the short wavelength end of the visible spectrum. It is one of the seven colors that Isaac Newton labeled when dividing the spectrum of visible light in 1704. Violet light has a wavelength between approximately 380 and 435 nanometers. The color's name is derived from the Viola genus of flowers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Amatista_Laye_2.jpg/330px-Amatista_Laye_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violet_(color)","wikidata":"Q428124"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Tulipa_alberti_Regel_-_PhytoKeys_%282024%29.jpg/500px-Tulipa_alberti_Regel_-_PhytoKeys_%282024%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Tulipa_alberti_Regel_-_PhytoKeys_%282024%29.jpg/1280px-Tulipa_alberti_Regel_-_PhytoKeys_%282024%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Tulipa_alberti_Regel_-_PhytoKeys_%282024%29.jpg/500px-Tulipa_alberti_Regel_-_PhytoKeys_%282024%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tulipa alberti in Kazakhstan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATulipa_alberti_Regel_-_PhytoKeys_(2024).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Tulipa_fringed_-_burgundy_lace_-_bulbs.jpg/500px-Tulipa_fringed_-_burgundy_lace_-_bulbs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Tulipa_fringed_-_burgundy_lace_-_bulbs.jpg/1280px-Tulipa_fringed_-_burgundy_lace_-_bulbs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Tulipa_fringed_-_burgundy_lace_-_bulbs.jpg/500px-Tulipa_fringed_-_burgundy_lace_-_bulbs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATulipa_fringed_-_burgundy_lace_-_bulbs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Tulipa_orphanidea_060506.jpg/500px-Tulipa_orphanidea_060506